+
+## 5. Findings
+
+Every failure or surprise gets a row; its triage id comes from the release checklist
+(`docs/internals/release-checklist.md`, RM/RS/RL).
+
+| Id | Found by | What | Triage |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| F-1 | P25-23 builder (reading release.yml, 2026-10-22) | The release workflow uploads only the desktop artefacts: `install.sh`, `install.ps1` and `install.cmd` are not attached to releases, yet the install guide and `install.cmd` download them from `releases/latest/download/…`. The smoke's `install` step fails until they are attached (for example: copy them from the admitted commit into the uploaded artefacts). | `<RM id>` |
+| F-2 | P25-23 builder | The desktop app has no licences screen; the notices file ships inside each package (the smoke checks the file). | `<RS/RL id>` |
+| F-3 | P25-23 builder | A script install has no built dashboard pages: `indus dashboard` builds them on first launch only when pnpm and Node are on the machine, otherwise only the API answers (`dashboard-login` fails). | `<RS id>` |
+| F-4 | P25-22 builder | A source install's `indus --version` prints the source tree's `0.0.0` (releases stamp the version into build trees only); the release it is on shows in `indus update --check` / `--plan`. | `<RS/RL id>` |
+| F-5 | P25-23 builder | Without a terminal, `indus chat -q` refuses a risky command when run `--local` (`approvals.single_query_mode`) but, attached to the daemon, leaves it waiting for an approval ("Resume the session in a terminal to answer it") and exits 3. Both are safe; the smoke accepts either. Decide whether the two should agree. | `<lead>` |
+| `<F-n>` | `<>` | `<>` | `<>` |
